+## Voyage 2 — DOM identity defect
+
+A real-browser Cypress acceptance suite found 10 failures caused by one root cause:
+`render()` destroys and recreates every `<li>` DOM node on every state change
+(`todoList.innerHTML = ''`), invalidating live element references.
+
+### What the acceptance suite catches
+
+1. **Toggle operations (tests 1-4)**: Clicking a checkbox calls `render()`, which rebuilds the
+   entire `<ul>`. The browser's element reference is now detached from the DOM.
+2. **Edit activation (tests 5-10)**: The dblclick handler sets `todo.editing = true` but calls
+   `render()` before saving to localStorage. `render()` reads `todos` from localStorage (where
+   `editing` was never persisted), so the new `<li>` lacks the `.editing` class. The `.edit`
+   input remains `display: none` per CSS, and `cy.clear()`/`cy.type()` fail.
+
+### Source-level conformance checks
+
+Eight `@source-conformance` scenarios in `features/dom-identity.feature` check the source
+code for forbidden patterns. They fail on the current `js/app.js` and must pass after the fix.
+
+### Required fix
+
+**Mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place** instead of rebuilding the list. Specifically:
+
+- `render()` must not assign to `todoList.innerHTML`. Use targeted DOM mutation (toggle
+  classes, update textContent, show/hide elements) on the existing `<li>` elements.
+- The toggle click handler must not call `render()`. Toggle `.completed` class and `.toggle.checked`
+  on the existing `<li>` directly, then call `setTodos()`.
+- The toggle-all handler must not call `render()`. Iterate existing `<li>` elements and toggle
+  each in place, then call `setTodos()`.
+- The dblclick handler must not call `render()`. Add `.editing` class to the existing `<li>`,
+  show `.edit` input, focus it, hide `.view`.
+- The commitEdit function must not call `render()`. Update the `<label>` textContent, remove
+  `.editing` class, hide `.edit`, show `.view`, then call `setTodos()`.
+- The escape handler must not call `render()`. Remove `.editing` class, restore original title,
+  hide `.edit`, show `.view`.
+- The destroy handler must not call `render()`. Remove the target `<li>` with
+  `li.parentNode.removeChild(li)`, then call `setTodos()`.
+- The clear-completed handler must not call `render()`. Remove completed `<li>` elements
+  in place, then call `setTodos()`.
+- The counter, footer visibility, toggle-all checkbox state, and filter link classes can be
+  updated via a lightweight `updateUI()` function that does not touch the todo list DOM.
+
+### Why happy-dom doesn't catch this
+
+happy-dom re-queries the DOM after every step, so detached element references are never
+observed. The `@source-conformance` tag guards the behaviour at the source level instead.
+
